{
  "$comment": "The eleven decision kinds that have effect in M1 (build spec §3) and the two D2 adds for M2 (A.7: `qualification_approval`, `trust_activation`; SEAM.md §117), each with what its preview must bind. Derived from D1 A.8 with build spec §6 corrections 5 and 22, RN R4, and the per-kind table of Review B12 and B18. `subject_types` is what the decision is about; `options` the keys it can offer (a decision offers a subset where SEAM.md says so); `manifest` the keys its `dependency_manifest` holds at least, each a value that the approval must be unable to drift across; `effect` whether consuming it records an effect intent whose preconditions are checked again immediately before a journaled operation is made (D1 §10.5). Stop and Abandon act through the run-end protocol and record none. Tests read expectations from this file, never from the engine. The key names are the Verifier's (SEAM.md §76). `effect_options` names the options of a kind marked `effect: false` whose positive answer nevertheless records an effect intent: `finding_disposition`'s `alpha_exception` writes `findings.alpha_exception` as an effect (D2 §5 C1; SEAM.md §119). M3 slice 19 (D3 §3.3; T10; SEAM.md §218): the three `check_correction_*` manifests also bind `classifier_version`, `classifier_authority` and the proposal's `discovery`. The two trust kinds are engine-scoped: their decision rows have no project, and they are read and answered through `GET /v1/decisions` and `POST /v1/decisions/:d/answer` (SEAM.md §117).",
  "codes": {
    "stale": "decision_stale",
    "consumed": "decision_consumed",
    "invalidated": "decision_invalidated",
    "batch_conflict": "batch_conflict",
    "intent_invalidated": "EFFECT_PRECONDITION_CHANGED"
  },
  "kinds": {
    "blocker": {
      "subject_types": ["work_item", "operation", "run"],
      "options": ["retry", "cancel", "continue", "acknowledge"],
      "manifest": ["subject_status", "quarantined", "cause", "evidence", "continuation"],
      "effect": false
    },
    "out_of_band_change": {
